Neural Networks (Moving Parts): license and attribution
=======================================================

This project contains two kinds of material with two different licenses, and
the distinction matters to anyone reusing it. The course content is adapted
from a NonCommercial source and carries that restriction. The application that
runs it, the series brand layer and course-kit/ are original work, contain none
of Nielsen's material, and are not covered by the grant below.

Course content (prose, pedagogical sequence, visualizations)
------------------------------------------------------------

Adapted from Michael A. Nielsen, "Neural Networks and Deep Learning",
Determination Press, 2015, licensed under the Creative Commons
Attribution-NonCommercial 3.0 Unported License (CC BY-NC 3.0):
https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc/3.0/

The course content, meaning the module prose, the pedagogical sequence and
the interactive figures under src/modules/, is offered under CC BY-NC 3.0 to
match its source: share and adapt it with attribution, for non-commercial
purposes only.

Note that CC BY-NC 3.0 has no ShareAlike clause, so this is a choice to match
the source rather than an obligation to. What does bind is narrower: no use of
Nielsen's material for commercial advantage, and no granting of rights in his
material beyond those held.

The application, the brand layer, and course-kit
------------------------------------------------

Everything under src/ other than src/modules/, together with src/brand/,
tools/ and course-kit/, is original work by the author. It contains none of
Nielsen's prose and none of his code, and the CC BY-NC grant above does not
extend to it.

No license is granted for it yet. That is a decision still to be made, not a
refusal, and until it is made these files are all rights reserved. Anyone who
wants to reuse the exercise harness, the Pyodide worker, the brand layer or
the kit should ask.


